		"output": "<span class='Z3988' title='url_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fzotero.org%3A2&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Adc&amp;rft.type=webpage&amp;rft.title=Pond%20-%20Pond&amp;rft.description=For%20secure%2C%20synchronous%20communication%20we%20have%20OTR%20and%2C%20when%20run%20over%20Tor%2C%20this%20is%20pretty%20good.%20But%20while%20we%20have%20secure%20asynchronous%20messaging%20in%20the%20form%20of%20PGP%20email%2C%20it&apos;s%20not%20forward%20secure%20and%20it%20gratuitously%20leaks%20traffic%20information.%20While%20a%20desire%20for%20forward%20secure%20PGP%20is%20hardly%20new%2C%20it%20still%20hasn&apos;t%20materialised%20in%20a%20widely%20usable%20manner.%0A%0AAdditionally%2C%20email%20is%20used%20predominately%20for%20insecure%20communications%20(mailing%20lists%2C%20etc)%20and%20is%20useful%20because%20it%20allows%20previously%20unconnected%20people%20to%20communicate%20as%20long%20as%20a%20(public)%20email%20address%20is%20known%20to%20one%20party.%20But%20the%20flip%20side%20to%20this%20is%20that%20volume%20and%20spam%20are%20driving%20people%20to%20use%20centralised%20email%20services.%20These%20provide%20such%20huge%20benefits%20to%20the%20majority%20of%20email%20communication%2C%20so%20it&apos;s%20unlikely%20that%20this%20trend%20is%20going%20to%20reverse.%20But%2C%20even%20with%20PGP%2C%20these%20services%20are%20trusted%20with%20hugely%20valuable%20traffic%20information%20if%20any%20party%20uses%20them.%0A%0ASo%20Pond%20is%20not%20email.%20Pond%20is%20forward%20secure%2C%20asynchronous%20messaging%20for%20the%20discerning.%20Pond%20messages%20are%20asynchronous%2C%20but%20are%20not%20a%20record%3B%20they%20expire%20automatically%20a%20week%20after%20they%20are%20received.%20Pond%20seeks%20to%20prevent%20leaking%20traffic%20information%20against%20everyone%20except%20a%20global%20passive%20attacker.&amp;rft.identifier=https%3A%2F%2Fpond.imperialviolet.org'></span>\n"
